Cogan: keep the stock KMI layout around BBRv3 where it can be kept (owner, 2026-10-22:
"Tetap BBRv3, versi lebih aman"). Applies on top of 004-bbrv3.patch and 005-bbr3-alias.patch
for the rothko stock kernel source (ACK android14-6.1-2025-06_r11, 6.1.138).

BBRv3 changed shared networking types, so 538 exported symbols used by the vendor modules
had other CRCs than the frozen ABI (r2/r3: force-load, 2498 "disagrees" lines at boot), and
it shifted struct net. Measured with the same compiler and config (local genksyms build):

- struct netns_ipv4: the five PLB sysctls move into its ANDROID_KABI_RESERVE(1) slot
  (ANDROID_KABI_USE). struct net is again 4096 bytes with ipv6 at 1408, as stock.
- struct tcp_sock: the two BBRv3 flags use spare bits of the same byte; genksyms sees the
  stock byte (#ifdef __GENKSYMS__). Same layout.
- enum tcp_ca_event: CA_EVENT_TLP_RECOVERY is appended; stock values are unchanged.
- struct rate_sample, struct tcp_congestion_ops: the BBRv3 members go after the stock ones
  and are hidden from genksyms. Stock offsets are unchanged and tcp_congestion_ops keeps its
  192-byte cache-line-aligned size; no vendor module implements a congestion control
  (tcp_register_congestion_control is in neither the mtk nor the xiaomi symbol list).

- struct tcp_bbr_info (UAPI inet_diag.h, union tcp_cc_info): the eleven BBRv3 fields stay
  after the stock ones and are hidden from genksyms. It is reached from struct sock
  through tcp_congestion_ops.get_info only in net/ipv4/tcp.c, whose exports
  tcp_sock_set_cork and tcp_sock_set_nodelay (mtk list) otherwise keep other CRCs (r4/r5:
  "CRC differs 2"); with it all 44 tcp.c CRCs equal stock (local genksyms, same compiler
  and config). The union is only passed by pointer; userspace reads it by length.

Left as is: icsk_ca_priv must hold BBRv3's 144-byte state (stock 104), so struct
inet_connection_sock and struct tcp_sock are 40 bytes larger and the tcp_* symbols that
reach them keep other CRCs. Sample of 905 symbols: 38 differ, none used by a vendor module
(BBR v1 baseline: 0; BBRv3 as carried by GKID: 428 of 672).

